<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a bug in the `pcap_findalldevs_ex` function in `pcap.c`. Specifically, the code does not handle the case where the `name` buffer is an empty string. This leads to `strlen(name)` (which is assigned to `stringlen`) returning 0. The subsequent access `name[stringlen - 1]` becomes `name[-1]`, which is a stack-buffer-underflow.

The fix is to add a check to ensure that `stringlen` is greater than 0 before accessing `name[stringlen - 1]`.

```c
// pcap.c:4757
stringlen = strlen(name);
if (stringlen > 0 && name[stringlen - 1] != ENDING_CHAR) {
// ...
}
```
</crash-analysis>

